ducerRunId":"run-24bb324e3f9e78e87dac7362df28ac94e6d068c351031aa03bd1a90261fe1a90","treeKind":"synthetic_merge"},"intendedChange":{"changedRequirements":[],"linkedIssues":["#10007","#11211","#11509","#12236"],"sources":["changeRequest.body","changeRequest.linkedIssues","changeRequest.title"],"status":"declared","title":"Merge menu extensions before filling unspecified fields"},"nextDecision":{"kind":"human_judgement","question":"Accept the change: the evidence is ready under the approved policy.","reason":"acceptance"},"preservedBehaviour":{"requirements":[{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-2JZT","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"The rewrite touches only the plain $(reader) form, mapping it to the captured slot. command -v reader, VAR=x reader, and every other form runs the real command."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"When no row is selectable, the menu shows no cursor at all rather than parking one on a row Enter cannot run. The cursor returns the moment a row becomes selectable."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","matchLevel":"function","obligations":["boundary","error_handling","input_domain"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"Unparseable input (after stripping), non-object JSON, and non-object entries yield an empty or skipped item set; no exception escapes the parser."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"title":"finishRequest with no active request or no done file just closes the menu. It creates or truncates no files."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"The menu discards a guard batch that exits nonzero or by signal, keeping the last complete result set in effect. An evaluation that stood aside runs once the process exits."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"An entry with action is an action, with target a link, otherwise a menu. An undeclared parent derives from the dotted id (or root). Root's parent is empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN"],"title":"open(payload) dispatches on mode: select/input open the dmenu flow, anything else opens the resolved route. close() cancels. refresh() reloads both JSONC files and returns ok. ping() returns ok."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-74BZ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"A route matching no id and no alias resolves to the literal input. A misspelling still attempts to open that id without a rewrite."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","matchLevel":"function","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"A user entry overrides the default per key while keeping the row's original order slot. The model injects a root item with label Go when no source declares one."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-6642","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-6642"],"title":"Delete with the cursor on an app row opens an uninstall confirmation naming the app. Confirming removes the app through the shared app library and closes the menu. Cancelling closes the dialog and returns focus without removing anything. Non-app rows ignore the key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN"],"title":"When the rows do not fit, the list height ends mid-row: the clipped peek row tells the eye there is more below the fold. The height never lands exactly on a row boundary, and the card never exceeds 70 percent of panel height."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"title":"finishRequest with a null selection (Escape/cancel) creates only the done file, so the caller observes the cancel as an empty selection."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"Absent an exact id, a route equal to a declared alias resolves to the id of the item declaring the alias. Alias comparison lowercases and maps underscores to dashes."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Drilling in pushes the previous menu on the navigation stack. Backspace/Left pops it, or falls back to the parent menu when the stack is empty. Entering a menu clears the filter."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"A row matches only when every query term appears in its name text (label, leaf id, aliases) or as a whole word in its description. Invisible and disabled rows never match."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","matchLevel":"function","obligations":["input_domain"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"The parser strips full-line // comments and trailing commas before JSON parsing, so the authored JSONC parses to its declared entries."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A"],"title":"swapProviderRows drops exactly the rows carrying the re-run provider's providerMenu and appends the new batch, leaving static children and other providers' rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5"],"title":"finishRequest with a selection writes the value to the selection file and creates the done file, shell-quoted, and only then closes."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"Applied guard results drive the view. A row hides when its when: is false. A static submenu or link hides when no descendant is visible, while provider-backed menus stay visible. A checked:true or disabled:true row earns the check-mark label. A disabled row dims and skips the cursor."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-MQ37","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"The generated guard script holds exactly one if-line per declared when, checked, or disabled, each echoing <id>:<w|c|d>:<0|1>; items with no guard get none."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-N3RM","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","SYS-REQ-260927-WC89"],"title":"When a route resolves to an action item with a non-empty action, the action runs directly and no menu opens."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"A dmenu option may lead with a glyph TAB and trail a subtext TAB. The picker shows the glyph but never returns it. A subtext-bearing pick returns 'label TAB subtext' as the stable key."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-PRNV","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"An exact id match wins over every alias. App rows are never routable, so an installed app's keywords cannot shadow a menu route (htop ships Keywords=system)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-RGCV","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"The prelude's omarchy-pkg-present/missing shadows agree with pacman -Q everywhere. This covers provides resolution, version constraints deferred to pacman, and the no-argument case (present true of nothing, missing not)."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"Scores tier exact label, whole-word app name, label prefix, label substring, name text, then description. Within a tier, menus and links move up by 2 and apps by 5, so an app outranks an equal menu row. Final order breaks ties by depth then declaration order."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6"],"title":"Search lists current-menu matches before deeper (drilldown) matches, with a divider section exactly when both groups are non-empty."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-W17G","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"A value command shared by several guards (e.g. omarchy-default-browser across seven rows) runs once per batch, captured eagerly before any guard line."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-XW52","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"When a route resolves to a link item, the menu opens at the link's target."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Y58B","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-47T8"],"title":"When no item declares a guard, the guard script is empty and no guard process runs."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Cursor movement lands on the next selectable row in the direction of travel, wrapping at the list ends. Movement steps over disabled rows."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z680","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["atomicity"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A"],"title":"mergeAppRows and swapProviderRows return fresh maps that drop orphan ids and the replaced batch. They list a duplicated incoming id once and never write into their input maps."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260928-8VJQ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["path_pair_agreement"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ"],"title":"A menu action may exactly match the bare-summon grammar: omarchy-shell shell summon <id>, plus an optional single-quoted payload. The payload carries no embedded quote and the id draws from [A-Za-z0-9._-]+. Such an action executes in-process via shell.summon(id, payload) instead of spawning bash. An absent payload defaults to an empty object literal, matching the bin/omarchy-shell argv default exactly. Any action outside that grammar falls back to the unchanged execDetached bash path. The fast path must preserve semantics: same plugin id, same payload bytes, same default."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["malformed_input"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW"],"title":"The merged item tree is addressable by id. An id present in the tree yields its item, and any other id yields null. Menu state then falls back to the root menu instead of a dangling entry."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-DXFJ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["edge_case"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-J0AN"],"title":"After the first filter keystroke or submenu move, the card top edge and the maximum rows height freeze at their current values. The card then grows and shrinks downward instead of re-centering on every resize. Closing the menu clears the freeze, so the next open centers again."},{"component":"menu","id":"SW-REQ-260929-T378","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["edge_case"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260922-P708"],"title":"Row selection follows the pointer only after it genuinely moves past the gate threshold. It never lands on a non-selectable row. Keyboard navigation, filtering, menu transitions, the delete dialog, and opening the menu disarm the gate. Synthetic hover churn under a stationary pointer therefore cannot move the selection."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-0M8A","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["atomicity"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"Dynamic rows (apps, provider enumerations) replace their source's previous batch atomically: orphans dropped, duplicates listed once, static rows untouched."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"Activating a row runs its action, follows its link, or drills into its submenu. The cursor never rests on a disabled row. Back navigation retraces the drill path."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-PPDW","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary","error_handling"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"The default JSONC and the user extension merge into one ordered item tree: per-key user overrides, stable order, inferred kinds and parents, injected root."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-R8DQ","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["boundary"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"A route string (exact id, declared alias, or normalized spelling) opens the item it denotes; unknown strings fall through as literal ids."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6","matchLevel":"file","parent":"STK-REQ-260922-XTNR","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260922-XTNR"],"title":"A filter query narrows to visible, selectable rows whose name or description matches every term, ranked by match quality."},{"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260927-WC89","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D"],"title":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee engages the session lock and exits 0. This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu."}],"total":41},"readiness":"ready","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:19ad4c0c6f4aa212c59917968707493bbf687a2badfa6754165c7cf20f03d281","policyRevision":"1e43373287afbd6dca4674ad463d5b5db7812358","role":"maintainer"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":41,"gatesAdvisory":27,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":178,"testsPassed":13},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbol` / line ranges (authored + derived) and function-local annotations; a whole-file trace is file-level (weak) and says nothing about which function a requirement needs.","Intent relations: requirement level = satisfies/parent or siblings under a parent with <= 20 children; component level = shared component (incl. traces.components); contract level = an interface requirement naming both components. A missing spec edge can make a real dependency look uncodified, and a broad contract can make an uncodified dependency look related — every candidate is a question for a reviewer, not a verdict on the code or the spec.","Removed-code traces: targets naming a removed/renamed/moved function or a deleted file, and requirement ids cited on removed diff lines that the evaluated file no longer cites. remainingTraces counts the requirement's other code targets at the evaluated revision without re-checking that each still resolves.","Renamed/moved detection is best effort: a removed and an added function with the same name in different files are \"moved\"; a different name with >= 80% identical normalized body lines (>= 3 lines) is \"renamed\"; anything else is removed + added.","Scope clusters are seeded only by directly touched requirements (spec changes and code_changed); behavior_affected requirements are what the change reaches and are judged by the uncodified-connection rule instead.","Uncodified connections need call-level impact (review.effects — C/C++ only today): this package has none, so NO uncodified connection could be detected. Absence of such candidates proves nothing here.","Units are function-granular only where a parser extracts function boundaries (tree-sitter languages, plus C/C++ function-like macros); other changed files are one file-granular unit, and hunks outside any function are attributed to the file only when no function of that file changed.","When a changed function is traced only at FILE level, every requirement of its file is a from-side seed: a relation through any of them counts as codified, so a coarse trace can MASK an uncodified connection (and inflate scope clusters — see coarse_trace)."],"changedFiles":4,"clusters":1,"coherence":"single","directRequirements":41,"mappingGranularity":"file","outOfScopeFiles":2,"reachedRequirements":0,"uncertaintyDisclosures":["effects_unavailable"],"unmappedFiles":0}},"dependencies":{"approximations":["runtime reach: the engine records no per-test or per-file execution trace; a code file the evaluation reaches only through calls, imports or sourcing, and a test with no declared link to the set, are not dependencies by this record (tests.ran still lists every test file the report names)","tests.ran lists the files the report's test cases name; when ranComplete is false some test case names no file","requirement and test files compare by git blob: any edit to the file (review stamps, a sibling requirement, a comment) counts as a change","config sections are the check descriptors' declarations (whole-manifest readers are listed under __manifest__); digests cover proof.yaml at the revision, not in-memory --set overrides","budgets assume additive counts: a requirement or variable that both the base and the change add is counted twice (an over-count)","records link by known-issue affected_requirements / affected_file / evidence_manifests, evidence results requirement / requirements / known_issues, and review subject / citations"],"budgets":[{"component":"menu","limit":100,"metric":"formalized_requirements","spec":"specs/software","used":57},{"component":"menu","limit":75,"metric":"guarantees","spec":"specs/software","used":57},{"component":"menu","limit":140,"metric":"variables","spec":"specs/software","used":127},{"component":"menu","limit":100,"metric":"formalized_requirements","spec":"specs/system","used":10},{"component":"menu","limit":75,"metric":"guarantees","spec":"specs/system","used":10},{"component":"m